# Unit tests for bacapp.c (run: python3 run_vectors.py tests.vec)
#
# Expected values are derived from ASHRAE 135 clause 20.2, not captured from the
# implementation.  Long outputs use the driver's <16 bytes>..<fnv1a64>/<len> form;
# those hashes were computed independently from the byte layout the standard gives.
#
# Implementation choices pinned by these tests (not dictated by the standard):
#   - bit-string encoder: any nonzero bits[i] is a 1 bit
#   - decoders accept non-minimal forms (leading-zero integers, short lengths in
#     extended form, tag numbers < 15 in extended form)
#   - decoders reject DATE/TIME field values the encoders reject
#   - application DOUBLE (tag 5) is rejected: bac_value_t has no slot for it

# ======================================================================= NULL / BOOLEAN
### null-encode null
enc_null
enc_null @1
enc_null @0
---
OK 00
OK 00
ERR
### boolean-encode boolean
enc_bool 0
enc_bool 1
enc_bool 0 @1
enc_bool 1 @0
---
OK 10
OK 11
OK 10
ERR
